  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-09-01T00:39:28.027Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For someone who has to manage a large friends list for hosting events, having a higher tier for 'Friends' would be a godsend. \nSometimes I just don't want other folks to be able to either see when I'm online, or even join on me specifically when I'm in a Friends+ world. Sometimes I just want to hang with a small group of people and only allow a small group of people to see what instance I'm in. It's tiring seeing most of your close friends be in a Invite+ world and have to send them requests just because there's no better option to managing who's allowed in the instance. \nHaving something like a 'Best/Close Friends' tier for specifically trusted folks would make gathering with close friends and seeing who's doing what be easier.\nHave it be a requested thing, just like Friends, where the other person has to consent to also putting said person on the Best Friends list. Even if they deny or later remove said person from Best Friends, they can still be allowed to be Friends.",
